-- title:
--   Theorem 4.5(iii) — every cluster point of e-PSG is a lifted stationary point
-- statement:
--   Let $S\subseteq\mathbb R^N$ be nonempty, closed and convex, and consider $\min_{x\in S} f(x)/g(x)$ under Assumptions 1 and 2. Choose the parameters of Step 1 of Algorithm 1 (e-PSG), let $(x_n)$ be a sequence generated by the algorithm, and suppose that $S_0=\{x\in S: f(x)/g(x)\le f(x_0)/g(x_0)\}$ is bounded and that $g$ is Lipschitz continuous around every point of $S$. If $\liminf_{n\to\infty}\tau_n=\bar\tau>0$, then every cluster point $\bar x$ of $(x_n)$ satisfies
--
--   1. $\bar x\in S\cap\operatorname{dom} f$;
--   2. $\displaystyle\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{f(x_n)}{g(x_n)}=\frac{f(\bar x)}{g(\bar x)}$;
--   3. $\bar x$ is a lifted stationary point of (P):
--   $$0\in g(\bar x)\,\partial_L(f+\iota_S)(\bar x)-f(\bar x)\,\partial_L g(\bar x).$$
--
--   This is the subsequential convergence guarantee of the extrapolated proximal subgradient method for nonconvex, nonsmooth fractional programs.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\liminf\tau_n>0$ is written as "there is $\bar\tau>0$ with $\tau_n\ge\bar\tau$ eventually", which is equivalent because $0<\tau_n\le1/\delta$. Cluster points are `MapClusterPt x̄ atTop x`. The hypothesis that $g$ is Lipschitz around every point of $S$ is a correction to the page: under the second alternative of Assumption 2 alone (regular and weakly convex on $S$) the printed statement fails, e.g. for $S=[0,1]$, $g(x)=2-\sqrt x$ on $S$, $f(x)=1-\sqrt x/4$, where the iterates converge to $0$ and $\partial_L g(0)=\emptyset$. Under the first alternative (weak convexity on an open convex set containing $S$) the hypothesis holds automatically, so for that alternative the statement is the page's.
-- source:
--   Boţ, Dao, Li, Extrapolated Proximal Subgradient Algorithms for Nonconvex and Nonsmooth Fractional Programs, arXiv:2003.04124v2, p. 11, Theorem 4.5(iii); proof pp. 12–13

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NonconvexSplitting_Shared_LimitingSubdiff
import Definitions.Def_NonconvexSplitting_Shared_StandingAssumptions
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Subseq_Basic
import Definitions.Def_FracPSG_Subseq_EPSG

open Filter Topology
open scoped InnerProductSpace

namespace FracPSG.Subseq

open NonconvexSplitting.Shared

/-- Theorem 4.5(iii) (Boţ–Dao–Li, arXiv:2003.04124v2, p. 11): under the hypotheses of Theorem 4.5,
if `liminf τₙ = τ̄ > 0` (here: `τₙ ≥ τ̄ > 0` eventually), then every cluster point `x̄` of the
iterates of Algorithm 1 lies in `S ∩ dom f`, `f(xₙ)/g(xₙ) → f(x̄)/g(x̄)`, and `x̄` is a lifted
stationary point of (P).

Correction to the page: `g` is assumed Lipschitz around every point of `S` (`hgLip`). Under the
second alternative of Assumption 2 alone the printed statement fails (`S = [0,1]`, `g = 2 − √x`
near `0`, where `∂_L g(0) = ∅`); under the first alternative `hgLip` holds automatically. -/
theorem theorem_4_5_iii
    {N : ℕ} {S : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N))}
    {fs : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) → ℝ} {fn : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) → EReal}
    {g : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N) → ℝ} {ℓ β δ ζ μbar κbar : ℝ}
    {x gs : ℕ → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N)} {τ κ μ : ℕ → ℝ}
    (hS : IsClosed S) (hSconv : Convex ℝ S)
    (hA1 : Assumption1 S fs fn ℓ) (hA2 : Assumption2 S g β)
    (hδ : 0 < δ) (hζ : 0 < ζ) (hβζ : 0 < 1 - Real.sqrt β * ζ) {m M : ℝ}
    (hpar : ParamsBC S (objF fs fn) g ℓ β δ ζ μbar κbar m M ∨ ParamsNoBC μbar κbar)
    (hrun : IsEPSGRun S fs fn g ℓ β δ ζ μbar κbar x gs τ κ μ)
    (hS0 : Bornology.IsBounded (S0 S (objF fs fn) g (x 0)))
    (hgLip : ∀ y ∈ S, ∃ K : NNReal, ∃ U ∈ 𝓝 y, LipschitzOnWith K g U)
    (hτ : ∃ τbar : ℝ, 0 < τbar ∧ ∀ᶠ n in atTop, τbar ≤ τ n) :
    ∀ xbar : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin N), MapClusterPt xbar atTop x →
      xbar ∈ S ∧ objF fs fn xbar ≠ ⊤ ∧
      Tendsto (fun n => ratio (objF fs fn) g (x n)) atTop
        (𝓝 (ratio (objF fs fn) g xbar)) ∧
      IsLiftedStationary (objF fs fn) g S xbar := by sorry

end FracPSG.Subseq
